In article <1615@hub.ucsb.edu> macross@banana.UUCP (David Christian) writes:
% 
% 	I would like to know what the ring of warning does too, (Well,
% yes, I know that it glows pink. Why? When?)
% 	And, sometimes the gods declare me the "Hand of Elbereth."  What are
% the benefits of this?

I don't know for sure (i.e., haven't read the source code) but common-sense
tells me that a ring of warning will warn me of bad things.  Such as monsters.
And the way it warns me is by glowing.  The intensity of the glow (a quali-
tative observation, I suppose) probably tells me how close the monster is.

As far as I'm concerned, getting to be the Hand of Elbereth is taking the 
easy way out.  Dump enough food on the gods, and pray and sooner or later
you're bound to become the HoE.  It means you get a lot of powers.  Let me
see...Fire resistance, Telepathy, Poison resistance, Intrinsic scare 
monster(?), your long-sword (if you are wielding it) gets named Excalibur,
etc.  The basic idea is that you come pretty close to becoming invincible,
and unless you do something really silly, the game should become a nice
walk through the park. 

Nuke it, I say.  More power to the novices, and the Gods be damned.  Enjoy.

